cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "dbound: a closed-form detectability bound for volumetric flaw inspection"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Yudong
    affiliation: "School of Mechanical Engineering, Heilongjiang University of Science and Technology, Harbin 150022, China"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3231-0444"
    email: 3468858545@qq.com
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24080212
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24080212"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24080213
    description: "version 0.1.0 (this specific release)"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An upper bound on the probability of detection of a volumetric flaw, derived
  from the Neyman-Pearson lemma and the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, with the
  cubic and three-halves-power asymptotes in the ratio of flaw size to voxel
  size, an inverse design rule, and a measured correction for clutter inflation
  on real X-ray computed tomography data. The twin decision layer of the
  AM-MultiModal-Monitoring system.
references:
  - type: software
    title: >-
      AM-MultiModal-Monitoring: an integrated in-situ monitoring system for metal
      additive manufacturing with a detectability bound
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Xbotsd/AM-MultiModal-Monitoring"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24128937
    notes: >-
      The measurement and application half of the pair; this package is vendored
      there at src/dbound and wrapped by ammonitor.decision.
  - type: dataset
    title: >-
      Tomographic image stacks for the study "Analysis of Porosity in AlSi10Mg
      Using Tomographic Image Processing"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.17602110
    license: CC-BY-4.0


